section: Academic warning
text:
Academic warning
Your CGPA is checked when each semester finishes, and your very first semester and summer terms are checked too. To stay clear of a warning you need at least 2.0 in a bachelor's programme, 2.5 in a master's programme or 3.0 in a PhD. Each time you finish below your line, you receive a warning and your warning count goes up by one. While you are on warning, you need permission from your Head of Department, or from a senior teacher the Head has chosen, before you can enrol again. Reaching the line or going above it resets your count to nothing. A third count ends your admission. Admission also ends by itself once you have used up the longest period allowed for finishing your degree.

