You may retake a course you have not passed, or one where you want a better grade. Anything you failed has to be taken again. If you are on warning, you must also retake passed courses whose grade points fall below the CGPA your programme requires. A master's student on warning, with a CGPA under 2.50, would need to retake courses scored below 2.50, which the rule illustrates as grades of C or C-.

